    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Tritone",
      "body": "Between the perfect 4th (5 half steps) and the perfect 5th (7) sits the **tritone**: 6 half steps, like C to F♯ or F to B.\n\n**Why it matters:** The tritone sounds tense, as if it wants to move. It sits inside the 7th chords that pull a song back home, which you will meet in Unit 6.",
